  "verbalization": "Phlorigidoside C is shown to have a direct target relationship with MIP, which is subsequently targeted by multiple compounds, including Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside and Tamarixinin B, all of which ultimately target HepG2. The evidence suggests that Phlorigidoside C may act through a common mechanism, targeting MIP, which is a key player in the biological response of HepG2 cells. The scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact mechanism by which MIP influences HepG2 remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple targets that share a common downstream effect supports the hypothesis that Phlorigidoside C may exert its effects through a shared pathway, potentially involving MIP. The integration of these findings highlights the potential for Phlorigidoside C to be a promising lead compound for targeting HepG2, provided further experimental validation of the mechanism is conducted.",
